  "theorem_transfer": {
    "application": "The selected reflections generate the infinite dihedral group. Every finite N-vertex subtree is a path; its union is a Coxeter fundamental polyhedron of a reflection subgroup of index N. Interiors are disjoint, so volume scales by N.",
    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.2140/gt.2006.10.737",
    "hypothesis_audited": "A doubling wall has only even finite Coxeter labels.  Two selected doubling walls need only be disjoint in H^10; parallel walls qualify even though their closures meet ideally.",
    "source": "Daniel Allcock, Infinitely many hyperbolic Coxeter groups through dimension 19, Geom. Topol. 10 (2006), Lemma 1.3, Theorem 4.1, and Corollary 4.2"
  }
